# duct-live -- the part of a live system that is not a program.
#
# Duct has no init system. Adding sysvinit or systemd is a decision with a long
# tail, and a live ISO does not need one: busybox init reads an inittab, keeps
# a shell alive on each console and runs one script at boot, which is the whole
# of what is required to get from switch_root to a prompt. This package is that
# inittab, that script, and the initramfs that hands control to them.
#
# Shell scripts and configuration files, identical on every architecture, so
# the Makefile builds it with --target any.
#
# No SRC_URL: there is nothing to fetch. The shared install.sh would try to run
# `make install` if SRC_DIR were set, so it is not set and this package brings
# its own install stage.
